WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.176
Three B links collaborative practice, Crew Resource Management, quality assurance and just culture. They are not separate slogans: each describes how a team prevents, detects or responds to failure.
3B把协作实践、团队资源管理、质量保证及公正文化连起来。它们不是彼此独立的口号，而是在说明团队如何预防、发现或处理失败。

00:00:13.176 --> 00:00:26.208
We will follow an original crew from the shift briefing through a changing trauma call and a simulated medication near miss. The cases rehearse the school objectives without using its assessed scenario bodies.
本课将跟随一支原创团队，从班前简报进入不断变化的创伤出诊，再经历一次模拟用药险失事件。案例演练学校目标，但不使用学校考核情境正文。

00:00:26.208 --> 00:00:36.240
The important performance is observable: a role is assigned, a concern is heard, an unsafe action stops and a report leads to a practical correction.
重要表现应可观察：角色得到分配，关注被听见，不安全行动被制止，报告带来实际修正。

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:49.488
Learning from an event does not remove accountability, and accountability does not require blaming a person for every bad outcome. Keep behavior, context and outcome distinct throughout this lesson.
从事件学习，不等于免除问责；问责也不需要为每个坏结局都责怪个人。本课始终区分行为、背景及结局。

00:00:49.488 --> 00:01:01.416
A crew may appear busy while important needs remain uncovered. One person sets up equipment, another asks a history and neither notices that no one owns the immediate airway problem.
团队可能看起来很忙，重要需要却仍无人负责。一人装器材，另一人问病史，却都没注意即时气道问题无人承担。

00:01:01.416 --> 00:01:12.624
The school contrasts simple side-by-side cooperation with true collaboration: coordinated work, clear communication and shared decision-making toward the patient's needs.
学校将简单并排合作与真正协作区分：真正协作是围绕患者需要，协调工作、清楚沟通并共同决策。

00:01:12.624 --> 00:01:22.560
A shared goal does not mean everyone performs the same task. It means the separate tasks fit together and the team can explain their priorities and dependencies.
共同目标不等于人人做同一件事，而是不同任务互相配合，团队说得清优先级及任务依赖。

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:33.504
Ask a partner to state the current objective in one sentence. If your answers differ materially, reconcile them before the mismatch produces a missed or duplicated action.
可请搭档用一句话说当前目标。若答案有实质差异，应先协调，避免不一致造成遗漏或重复。

00:01:33.504 --> 00:01:42.456
Name the person and the task instead of announcing that someone should do it. Include the immediate priority and the relevant safety constraint.
应点名并说任务，不能只说“应该有人去做”。应包括即时优先级及相关安全限制。

00:01:42.456 --> 00:01:51.504
The receiver acknowledges and clarifies uncertainty. An assigned task without acknowledgement may exist only in the leader's mind.
接收者应确认并澄清不确定。任务无人确认，可能只存在于负责人的脑中。

00:01:51.504 --> 00:02:00.024
The leader monitors whether the workload is feasible and whether the patient has changed. Delegating a task does not mean the leader can forget it.
负责人应监测工作量是否可行，以及患者是否变化。分派不等于此后就能忘掉该任务。

00:02:00.024 --> 00:02:12.048
Completion, inability to perform and a new hazard all return to the team. Reassign explicitly when roles change so that ongoing care does not silently lose its owner.
完成、无法执行及新危险，都应回报团队。角色改变时应明确重分配，避免持续照护悄悄变成无人负责。

00:02:12.048 --> 00:02:22.440
A shared mental model is a common understanding of the patient, risks and plan. It is not a demand that all team members hold the same unchanging diagnosis.
共享心智模型是对患者、风险及方案的共同理解，不是要求所有人固守同一个不变诊断。

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:35.016
In the original trauma call, one clinician notices worsening pallor and a weaker pulse while the other is completing a secondary survey. Without an update, they are treating two different mental patients.
原创创伤出诊中，一人发现苍白加重及脉搏变弱，另一人仍在完成次级评估。若不更新，他们实际上在照护两个不同的“脑中患者”。

00:02:35.016 --> 00:02:46.584
Announce the new finding and its significance, then state the revised priority. Confirm who continues support, who requests resources and how the movement plan changes.
应宣布新发现及意义，再说调整后优先级。确认谁继续支持、谁求援，以及搬运方案如何变化。

00:02:46.584 --> 00:02:56.112
Invite a challenge to the new explanation. A shared model is useful because it is visible and revisable, not because it prevents disagreement.
应邀请对新解释提出质疑。共享模型之所以有用，是因为公开且可修订，而不是消除分歧。

00:02:56.112 --> 00:03:07.248
Situational awareness includes the patient, the environment and the crew. A monitor may remain stable while an exit becomes blocked or a partner becomes overwhelmed.
情境意识包括患者、环境及团队。即使监护数值稳定，出口仍可能被堵，搭档也可能已经超负荷。

00:03:07.248 --> 00:03:17.640
Watch for fixation on a procedure or diagnosis. If both clinicians are occupied with the same detail, ask who is watching the broader patient and scene.
应注意对某操作或诊断的固着。两人都盯同一细节时，应问谁还在观察整体患者及现场。

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:30.024
Share uncertainty early and anticipate the next likely need. A short request for help before overload is safer than silently falling behind until a critical task is missed.
应及早分享不确定，并预判下一需要。在超负荷前简短求助，比默默落后直到漏掉关键任务更安全。

00:03:30.024 --> 00:03:41.952
Use protocols and team input to make timely decisions, then reassess the result. Awareness without an action or plan update is only noticing, not effective CRM.
应使用规程及团队意见及时决策，并重评结果。只有注意到问题却不行动或更新方案，不算有效团队资源管理。

00:03:41.952 --> 00:03:53.208
A leader gives direction while admitting limits and inviting information. Saying please tell me if I miss something is useful only when the response to a real concern is respectful.
负责人应给方向，同时承认局限并邀请信息。只有真正有人提关注时仍尊重回应，“我漏了请提醒”才有用。

00:03:53.208 --> 00:04:04.632
Followership is not silent obedience. It includes completing tasks, reporting changes, supporting the plan and challenging a safety problem regardless of experience or rank.
跟随不是沉默服从，而包括完成任务、报告变化、支持方案，并不论资历或级别都指出安全问题。

00:04:04.632 --> 00:04:17.232
Flattening hierarchy reduces the barrier to speaking up; it does not abolish clinical responsibility or expand anyone's scope. Keep the responsible roles and required supervision clear.
降低等级障碍是减少开口阻力，不是取消临床责任或扩大权限。负责人角色及所需督导仍须清楚。

00:04:17.232 --> 00:04:29.136
When a junior member is right about a hazard, acknowledge the contribution and change the plan. Defending status at the expense of patient safety teaches the crew to hide the next concern.
新人对危险判断正确时，应认可贡献并改变方案。为了维护地位而牺牲安全，只会教团队下次隐藏关注。

00:04:29.136 --> 00:04:41.304
The module includes police, fire, hospital staff and appropriate bystanders in collaborative practice. Each may hold information or expertise that the ambulance crew does not.
模块将警察、消防、医院人员及适当旁人纳入协作实践。他们可能掌握救护团队没有的信息或专业能力。

00:04:41.304 --> 00:04:52.344
Explain the patient's need and listen to the other discipline's constraints. An urgent care request and a rescue hazard must be reconciled into a workable sequence.
应说明患者需要，并听取其他专业限制。紧急照护请求与救援危险，需协调成可执行顺序。

00:04:52.344 --> 00:05:03.360
Respect does not mean avoiding a difficult conversation. Describe a specific conflict and seek a patient-centered solution rather than accusing another agency of not caring.
尊重不代表回避困难对话。应描述具体冲突并寻求以患者为中心的方案，而不是指责另一机构不关心患者。

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:13.680
Confirm who owns the next step and communicate any delay or changed risk. Several agencies working hard do not guarantee that the critical task has an owner.
应确认谁负责下一步，并沟通延误或风险变化。多个机构都很努力，不保证关键任务就有人负责。

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:23.592
A brief safety huddle makes important information visible before pressure increases. Discuss readiness, known limitations and who can provide help.
简短安全碰头可在压力增大前让重要信息可见。应讨论准备状态、已知局限及谁能提供帮助。

00:05:23.592 --> 00:05:34.176
Identify missing or unreliable equipment through the actual service process. Do not let an informal workaround silently become the crew's accepted standard.
应按真实服务流程指出缺失或不可靠器材。不能让非正式变通悄悄成为团队默认标准。

00:05:34.176 --> 00:05:44.736
Agree on roles and likely hazards, while leaving room for new information. A briefing is a starting model, not a script that must survive every change.
应约定角色及可能危险，同时给新信息留空间。简报是起始模型，不是无论如何变化都必须照走的剧本。

00:05:44.736 --> 00:05:54.624
Ask directly for uncertainty and thank the person who raises it. Repeated respectful responses make psychological safety credible in daily work.
应直接邀请说出不确定，并感谢提出者。日常持续尊重回应，才能让心理安全可信。

00:05:54.624 --> 00:06:08.400
The tools overlap, but they are not interchangeable acronyms. Choose one based on whether the problem is a task, critical information, an urgent change, a structured update or an unheard safety concern.
工具可重叠，却不是可随便互换的缩写。应先判断问题是任务、关键信息、紧急变化、结构化更新，还是未被听见的安全关注。

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:19.056
A long SBAR is not the first response to a medicine about to be administered incorrectly. A direct stop can protect the patient, followed by a structured explanation.
药物即将错误给入时，冗长SBAR不是首要反应。先直接制止可保护患者，随后再结构化解释。

00:06:19.056 --> 00:06:29.040
Likewise, a shouted callout does not replace the detailed handover needed at transfer. The receiver needs enough context to continue care safely.
同样，大声通报不能替代转交时所需详细交接。接收者需要足够背景，才能安全延续照护。

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:38.424
Practice the actual words with a partner. Knowing an acronym's expansion is not evidence that you can use the tool under interruption or noise.
应与搭档练真实措辞。知道缩写全称，不证明在打断或噪声下就能使用。

00:06:38.424 --> 00:06:48.240
Use a named receiver and a specific request. For an original example: Alex, obtain a repeat manual blood pressure and report it now.
应点名接收者并给具体请求。原创例子是：Alex，现在复测手动血压并报告。

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:57.528
The receiver repeats the essential task, and the sender confirms or corrects it. This catches a misheard action before it becomes a wrong action.
接收者复述关键任务，发送者确认或纠正。这样可在听错变成做错前截住。

00:06:57.528 --> 00:07:07.968
When completed, report the actual result and any problem. If the measurement cannot be obtained, report that instead of silently attempting forever.
完成后应报真实结果及问题。若测不到，应说明，不能一直默默尝试。

00:07:07.968 --> 00:07:16.728
Read-back confirms the message, not the clinical appropriateness of the instruction. A correctly repeated unsafe plan must still be questioned.
复述核对确认的是信息，不是指令在临床上适当。即使正确复述，不安全方案仍须质疑。

00:07:16.728 --> 00:07:27.960
In a simulated medication task, two people repeat the same volume but neither reads the concentration. The communication is consistent, yet the clinical check has failed.
模拟给药中，两人都重复相同体积，却无人读浓度。沟通虽然一致，临床核查却失败了。

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:37.896
An independent check uses the original patient, order or protocol and actual product information. It does not start by accepting the first person's answer.
独立核查须使用原始患者、指示或方案，以及真实产品信息，不能先接受第一人的答案再开始。

00:07:37.896 --> 00:07:49.056
Read back critical numbers with units and clarify ambiguity. Dose, concentration and volume answer different questions even when one number happens to look familiar.
关键数字复述应带单位，并澄清歧义。即使某个数看着熟悉，药量、浓度及体积仍是在回答不同问题。

00:07:49.056 --> 00:07:57.648
Use both tools where required: confirm the message and verify the plan. Team agreement is not a substitute for evidence.
按需要同时使用两种工具：确认信息，也核实方案。团队都同意，不能替代证据。

00:07:57.648 --> 00:08:07.200
A callout is a brief direct statement of an urgent need or change. It helps the team notice information that might otherwise remain with one person.
紧急通报是对迫切需要或变化的简短直接表述，可让团队注意原本可能只在一人手中的信息。

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:19.632
In the trauma case, say that the patient is less responsive and the pulse is weaker, then request immediate reassessment and the relevant support. Avoid a vague announcement that things look bad.
创伤案例中，应说患者反应下降、脉搏更弱，再请求立即重评及有关支持。不要只模糊说“情况不好”。

00:08:19.632 --> 00:08:30.072
Acknowledge the callout and state the change in plan. If no one responds, the sender should verify it was heard rather than assuming silence means agreement.
接收后应确认并说明方案变化。若无人回应，发送者应核实是否听到，不能把沉默当同意。

00:08:30.072 --> 00:08:40.392
Keep the tone calm and the content concise. Urgency is carried by clear findings and action, not by humiliation or competing shouts.
语气应平静，内容应简洁。紧急性来自清楚发现及行动，不是羞辱或互相喊叫。

00:08:40.392 --> 00:08:48.984
Lead with the current problem and urgency. A listener should not need to wait through a long history to discover that the patient is deteriorating.
应先说当前问题及紧急程度。听者不应听完长病史，才知道患者正在恶化。

00:08:48.984 --> 00:08:57.528
Give the background that changes the decision, then your assessment and evidence. Separate what you measured from what you think it means.
应提供会改变决定的背景，再说评估及证据，并区分测得事实与解释。

00:08:57.528 --> 00:09:07.368
Include treatment and response, not only the first set of observations. Make a specific recommendation or request within the actual clinical pathway.
应包括治疗及反应，不能只报首组观察。应在真实临床路径内作具体建议或请求。

00:09:07.368 --> 00:09:19.320
Confirm the response and clarify uncertain instructions. SBAR organizes communication; it does not grant a new treatment authority or guarantee that a message was received.
应确认回应，并澄清不确定指示。SBAR只是组织沟通，不赋予新治疗权限，也不保证对方已收到。

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:29.352
The school PACE model expands to Probe, Alert, Challenge and Emergency. It is a graded-assertiveness tool for an unresolved safety concern.
学校PACE是Probe、Alert、Challenge及Emergency，即探询、提醒、挑战及紧急制止，用于未解决安全关注的分级表达。

00:09:29.352 --> 00:09:39.192
Use progressively explicit language if the concern is not addressed. Name the risk and the action needed instead of repeating an increasingly frustrated hint.
关注未被处理时，应逐步更明确表达。应说出风险及所需行动，而不是反复更生气地暗示。

00:09:39.192 --> 00:09:48.984
The goal is safe action, not winning a disagreement. Once the unsafe step is paused, verify the facts together and revise the plan.
目标是安全行动，不是争赢。暂停不安全步骤后，应共同核查事实并修订方案。

00:09:48.984 --> 00:09:58.200
The stages are not a mandatory slow sequence. If a harmful administration is imminent, use the direct emergency stop immediately.
这些阶段不是必须慢慢走的顺序。若有害给药即将发生，应立刻直接紧急制止。

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:07.920
In the original near-miss case, the junior partner notices a concentration mismatch while the senior clinician is preparing to deliver a simulated medicine.
原创险失案例中，资历较浅搭档发现浓度不符，而资深临床人员正准备给入模拟药物。

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:19.656
The safe response is to pause and hear the concern, not to defend experience. A statement that anyone may speak up is meaningless if the first actual challenge is punished.
安全回应是暂停并听关注，而不是捍卫经验。如果第一次真实质疑就受惩罚，“任何人都能开口”只是空话。

00:10:19.656 --> 00:10:29.424
Check the source information, product, intended amount and patient before resuming. Do not merely change the volume to the second person's guess.
恢复前应核原始信息、产品、目标药量及患者。不能只是把体积改成第二人的猜测。

00:10:29.424 --> 00:10:40.128
Acknowledge the intercept and report the near miss through the appropriate process. The team protected this patient, but the confusing system may remain for the next crew.
应认可截获，并通过适当流程报告险失事件。团队保护了本患者，但混淆系统可能仍会影响下一团队。

00:10:40.128 --> 00:10:50.640
Conflict language should describe a specific behavior or unresolved fact. General attacks invite a dispute about personality instead of correcting the action.
冲突措辞应描述具体行为或未解决事实。泛化攻击容易变成人格争论，而不是纠正行动。

00:10:50.640 --> 00:11:00.624
Use an observation, a concern and a clear request. The request should say what needs to happen now, not merely express dissatisfaction.
可用观察、关注及明确请求。请求应说现在要做什么，而不只是表达不满。

00:11:00.624 --> 00:11:10.560
Respectful language can still be firm. Immediate safety does not require an apologetic hint, especially after a clear concern has been ignored.
尊重仍可坚定。即时安全不需要带歉意暗示，特别是在明确关注已被忽视后。

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:21.456
Resolve the urgent hazard first and address broader disagreement afterward through the appropriate channel. Do not turn an active clinical problem into a prolonged argument.
先解决紧急危险，再通过适当渠道处理更广分歧。不能把正在发生的临床问题拖成长时间争吵。

00:11:21.456 --> 00:11:32.592
Give feedback soon enough to be useful and focus on an observed action. Explain its consequence and a practical next step rather than judging the person's character.
反馈应及时到仍有用，并聚焦可观察行动。说明后果及可行下一步，而不是评价人格。

00:11:32.592 --> 00:11:42.168
When receiving feedback, listen and ask what specifically was observed. You can clarify context without treating every concern as a personal attack.
接收反馈时，应听并问具体观察到了什么。可以澄清背景，不必把每项关注视为个人攻击。

00:11:42.168 --> 00:11:56.592
Acknowledge useful information and identify a change you can demonstrate. If a proposed correction conflicts with the actual protocol or device, resolve that evidence rather than agreeing politely and remaining confused.
应认可有用信息，并指出能展示的改变。若建议修正与真实方案或器材冲突，应核证据，不能礼貌同意却继续困惑。

00:11:56.592 --> 00:12:06.552
Repeat the relevant sequence and check whether performance changes. A friendly debrief is valuable, but the safety target is a more reliable action.
应重做相关顺序并检查表现是否改变。友善复盘有价值，但安全目标是让行动更可靠。

00:12:06.552 --> 00:12:18.216
The school uses the Swiss Cheese Model to explain interacting weaknesses across defensive layers. A final wrong action may be visible while the contributing conditions are less obvious.
学校用瑞士奶酪模型解释防御层之间相互作用的弱点。最后错误动作很显眼，但促成条件可能不明显。

00:12:18.216 --> 00:12:31.992
In the original near miss, similar labels, crowded storage, interrupted checking and an authority gradient all matter. Correcting only the person at the syringe may leave the same trap in place.
原创险失中，相似标签、拥挤存放、核查被打断及等级障碍都重要。只纠正拿注射器的人，可能仍留下同一陷阱。

00:12:31.992 --> 00:12:44.328
System analysis does not mean every event has identical causes or no individual responsibility. Investigate the actual event rather than forcing every detail into a diagram.
系统分析不代表每件事成因相同，也不代表个人无责任。应调查真实事件，不能硬把每个细节塞进图。

00:12:44.328 --> 00:12:57.024
Ask which defenses existed, why they did not work and what could reliably interrupt recurrence. More reminders alone may be weaker than correcting confusing storage or unavailable equipment.
应问有哪些防御、为何失效，以及什么能可靠阻止再发。单纯更多提醒，可能不如修正混淆存放或器材不可用。

00:12:57.024 --> 00:13:08.208
A layered approach reduces reliance on one perfect person or one perfect check. Design, preparation, communication and learning each contribute something different.
多层方法可减少对一个完美人员或一次完美核查的依赖。设计、准备、沟通及学习，各自提供不同作用。

00:13:08.208 --> 00:13:20.616
The layers are not automatically independent. If two clinicians rely on the same wrong assumption or unreadable label, two signatures may still represent one shared failure.
各层不会自动互相独立。若两人都依同一错误假设或看不清标签，两份签名仍可能只是同一次共享失败。

00:13:20.616 --> 00:13:31.104
Choose a correction that addresses the observed cause, and test whether it creates another problem. Moving a product may reduce one confusion but make urgent access harder.
应选择针对观察成因的修正，并检验是否制造其他问题。挪动产品可减少一种混淆，却也可能让紧急取用更困难。

00:13:31.104 --> 00:13:40.968
Use follow-up information to refine the change. The purpose of the model is better care, not a visually satisfying explanation that no one evaluates.
应用后续信息完善改变。模型的目的是更好照护，不是做出一张好看却无人检验的解释图。

00:13:40.968 --> 00:13:53.832
Quality assurance is structured review of whether care meets expected standards, using records, audits, peer review and incident information. It is more than finding a person to criticize.
质量保证是使用记录、审核、同伴评议及事件信息，结构化审视照护是否符合预期标准，不只是找个人批评。

00:13:53.832 --> 00:14:07.200
Your role includes complete patient records, timely safety reports, honest debriefs and receptiveness to feedback. A missing record can hide both an unsafe process and a successful defense.
你的角色包括完整患者记录、及时安全报告、诚实复盘及接受反馈。缺失记录可同时掩盖不安全过程及成功防御。

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:18.360
Ask how the findings lead to action and who owns follow-up. Repeatedly discussing the same near miss without changing the process is not a completed improvement cycle.
应问发现如何变成行动，以及谁负责后续。反复讨论同类险失却不改变流程，不算完成改进循环。

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:30.720
Interpret report counts carefully. More reports may reflect better willingness to speak up, not necessarily more underlying harm; compare the reporting process and relevant care measures.
报告数量应谨慎解释。更多报告可能是更愿意开口，不一定代表更多真实伤害；应结合报告过程及有关照护指标比较。

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:41.736
The school repeatedly describes a near miss as intercepted before reaching the patient, but its glossary also says before harm. Those are not identical thresholds.
学校多次把险失描述为到达患者前被截获，但词汇表又写成伤害发生前。两个门槛并不相同。

00:14:41.736 --> 00:14:53.784
The WHO terminology separates a near miss, which did not reach the patient, from a no-harm incident, which reached the patient without discernible harm. A harmful incident causes harm.
WHO术语区分：未到达患者的是险失；已到达但无可辨伤害的是无伤害事件；造成伤害的则是伤害事件。

00:14:53.784 --> 00:15:06.912
An error can be caught before administration or can reach the patient. Do not define all errors as necessarily reaching the patient, and do not infer no harm merely because the first observation is reassuring.
错误可在给入前被发现，也可到达患者。不能把所有错误都定义成必已到达，也不能因首轮观察尚好就断定无伤害。

00:15:06.912 --> 00:15:17.376
Use the actual reporting system's fields while describing the event precisely. Do not relabel a wrong administration as a near miss just because the patient survived.
应依真实报告系统字段填写，同时精确描述事件。不能因为患者存活，就把错误给入改称险失。

00:15:17.376 --> 00:15:30.264
Human error is an unintentional slip, lapse or mistake. A competent person may misread a confusing label or omit a step during interruption despite intending to follow the correct process.
人为错误是非故意失手、疏漏或判断错误。有能力的人即使本想遵循正确流程，也可能误读混淆标签，或在打断中漏步。

00:15:30.264 --> 00:15:39.744
Understand what information and conditions existed at the time. Hindsight can make an ambiguous situation seem much clearer than it was to the provider.
应了解当时信息及条件。事后看来，原本模糊的情况往往显得比当时清楚。

00:15:39.744 --> 00:15:50.760
The school response is to support or console the provider, learn and correct system contributions. Support is compatible with an honest report and appropriate review.
学校对应处理是支持或安慰人员、学习，并修正系统促成因素。支持可以与诚实报告及适当审查并存。

00:15:50.760 --> 00:16:01.416
Do not classify intent from the severity of the outcome alone. The same unintentional action may have no harm in one case and severe consequences in another.
不能仅凭结局严重程度判断意图。同样非故意动作，在一个病例无伤害，另一个却可能后果严重。

00:16:01.416 --> 00:16:13.968
At-risk behavior is a choice that increases risk when the risk is not recognized or seems justified. A repeated shortcut may feel normal because it has not yet caused a visible injury.
风险行为是增加风险的选择，但当事人未认识风险，或认为风险有理由。某捷径尚未造成明显伤害，就可能被反复当作正常。

00:16:13.968 --> 00:16:24.264
The module gives prematurely abbreviated assessment as an example. Investigate why the shortcut made sense to the person and what workload or rewards may encourage it.
模块举提前缩短评估为例。应调查当事人为何觉得合理，以及哪些工作量或奖励在鼓励捷径。

00:16:24.264 --> 00:16:36.408
Use coaching and clear expectations, while correcting the conditions that reward the unsafe choice. Education alone may fail if the workflow makes the safe method impractical.
应指导并明确期待，同时修正奖励不安全选择的条件。若工作流让安全做法不可行，仅教育可能失败。

00:16:36.408 --> 00:16:46.320
Do not automatically call every intentional deviation reckless. Context, risk awareness and the actual choice require fair review.
不能把每次有意偏离都自动叫鲁莽。背景、风险认识及真实选择，都需要公正审查。

00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:58.704
The school defines reckless behavior as conscious disregard of a substantial unjustifiable risk. This is different from an unintentional mistake or a shortcut whose risk was not appreciated.
学校把鲁莽行为定义为有意识漠视重大且无正当理由的风险，区别于非故意错误或未认识风险的捷径。

00:16:58.704 --> 00:17:09.552
If an immediate safety threat is present, protect patients and colleagues through the appropriate process. Do not wait for a later learning discussion before stopping unsafe practice.
若存在即时安全威胁，应通过适当流程保护患者及同事。不能等日后学习讨论，才制止不安全执业。

00:17:09.552 --> 00:17:20.904
Formal review and corrective or disciplinary action may be required. The course is not an authority for a partner to deliver an instant legal verdict or an employment sanction.
可能需要正式审查及纠正或纪律行动。但本课不赋予搭档当场法律定罪或就业处分的权力。

00:17:20.904 --> 00:17:31.608
Evidence and context matter regardless of seniority. A good outcome does not make a reckless choice safe, just as a bad outcome does not prove recklessness.
无论资历，证据及背景都重要。好结局不会让鲁莽选择变安全，坏结局也不证明鲁莽。

00:17:31.608 --> 00:17:43.104
Just culture seeks learning and appropriate accountability. It distinguishes behavior and system contributions instead of responding only to the outcome or the person's reputation.
公正文化追求学习及适当问责，区分行为与系统因素，不只按结局或个人名声回应。

00:17:43.104 --> 00:17:56.352
Psychological safety means people can raise concerns, ask questions and admit uncertainty without humiliation or automatic blame. It does not remove professional responsibilities.
心理安全意味着能提出关注、问问题及承认不确定，而不受羞辱或自动责怪；它不取消专业责任。

00:17:56.352 --> 00:18:09.624
Do not promise that every report has no consequences or that all discussion is legally privileged. Follow the actual reporting and review policy, with fair treatment and appropriate support.
不能保证每次报告都无后果，也不能称所有讨论都有法律保密特权。应遵循真实报告及审查政策，同时公正对待并提供适当支持。

00:18:09.624 --> 00:18:21.072
The strongest practical signal is what happens after a real concern: a respectful pause, accurate review, visible correction and feedback to the people who reported.
最有力的实际信号，是一次真实关注之后发生什么：尊重地暂停、准确审查、可见修正，以及向报告者反馈。

00:18:21.072 --> 00:18:30.960
A simulated syringe has been prepared using the wrong assumed concentration. The partner identifies the mismatch before any simulated medication is delivered.
一支模拟注射器按错误假定浓度备好，搭档在任何模拟药物给入前发现不符。

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:42.240
Pause, verify the patient and source information, and restore a correct authorized preparation. Do not continue because the error was only a small calculation issue.
应暂停，核患者及原始信息，并恢复正确获准准备。不能因“只是小计算问题”而继续。

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:53.160
This is a near miss because the incident did not reach the patient. The intercept is a successful defense, but the confusing concentration or storage still needs attention.
因为事件未到达患者，这是险失。截获是成功防御，但混淆浓度或存放仍需处理。

00:18:53.160 --> 00:19:03.240
Report through the appropriate safety process and include what enabled the intercept. Learning from what worked is as important as describing the initial failure.
应通过适当安全流程报告，并写明什么促成截获。学习有效防御，与描述最初失败同样重要。

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:14.688
Change one variable: the mismatch is noticed after some simulated medicine has already entered. The event has reached the patient even if the person initially looks unchanged.
只改变一个变量：部分模拟药物已经进入，才发现不符。即使患者最初看似未变，事件也已到达患者。

00:19:14.688 --> 00:19:30.576
Stop the implicated delivery as appropriate, assess and support the patient, and determine the actual product, concentration, amount and time. Uncertain delivery is stated as uncertain, not rounded into a reassuring number.
应按情况停止有关给入、评估及支持患者，并确认真实产品、浓度、药量及时间。不确定给入量应如实说不确定，不能凑成安心数字。

00:19:30.576 --> 00:19:42.360
Obtain the appropriate urgent clinical guidance and monitoring. Reversal is substance-specific and may not exist; do not improvise an antidote or wait for harm before seeking help.
应取得适当紧急临床指导及监测。逆转处理取决于具体物质，也可能根本不存在；不能临时发明解药，或等伤害出现才求助。

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:54.480
If no discernible harm is established, it is a no-harm incident under the stated terminology, not a near miss. Harm and later evolution still require appropriate evaluation.
若确认没有可辨伤害，依所述术语是无伤害事件，而不是险失。伤害及后续演变仍需适当评估。

00:19:54.480 --> 00:20:05.208
The first priority after recognizing an error is patient safety. Address the implicated action and immediate clinical need before treating the event as paperwork.
发现错误后，第一优先是患者安全。应先处理有关行动及即时临床需要，不能先把它当文书问题。

00:20:05.208 --> 00:20:19.728
Notify the appropriate clinical and supervisory resources promptly, with enough detail for useful advice. Consultation should be concurrent with necessary immediate support, not a reason to leave the patient unattended.
应及时通知适当临床及督导资源，并给足够细节以取得有用建议。咨询应与必要即时支持并行，不能让患者无人照护。

00:20:19.728 --> 00:20:32.040
Communicate honestly with the patient or appropriate authorized person through the actual disclosure process. Do not delay urgent care while trying to settle blame or a complete causal explanation.
应通过真实披露流程，向患者或适当获授权者诚实沟通。不能为确定责怪对象或完整成因而延误紧急照护。

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:44.712
Then complete patient documentation and the separate safety report, participate in review and use available support. Protecting future patients requires a follow-through beyond the immediate recovery.
随后应完成患者文书及另行安全报告、参与审查，并使用可用支持。要保护未来患者，不能只做到即时补救。

00:20:44.712 --> 00:20:55.272
Use plain compassionate language to explain what is known and the immediate care plan. Acknowledge uncertainty and answer questions honestly within your role.
应以平实且有同理心的语言说明已知情况及即时照护方案。承认不确定，并在角色范围内诚实回答。

00:20:55.272 --> 00:21:10.488
The school includes disclosure as part of responding to errors and near misses. The actual scope and process, including near-miss disclosure, must follow applicable organizational guidance; do not invent one universal script.
学校把披露纳入错误及险失处理。但实际范围及流程，包括险失披露，应遵循适用机构指引，不能虚构统一通用稿。

00:21:10.488 --> 00:21:21.840
Family involvement depends on the patient's wishes, capacity and the applicable authority. A relative being present is not automatic permission to share every clinical detail.
家属参与取决于患者意愿、能力及适用权限。亲属在场，不代表可自动披露每个临床细节。

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:31.032
Do not speculate about another person's motives or promise that there will be no harm. Explain the assessment and follow-up while the facts are established.
不能猜测他人动机，也不能保证绝无伤害。在事实核实过程中，应解释评估及后续。

00:21:31.032 --> 00:21:43.776
Record the actual administration, observations, actions, response and relevant consultations. Saying only medication given hides the information the next clinician needs.
应记真实给入、观察、行动、反应及相关咨询。只写“已给药”，会藏住下一位临床人员所需信息。

00:21:43.776 --> 00:21:55.296
Objective language means accurate facts and attributed information, not removing the fact that an incorrect amount was delivered. Reasoned clinical concerns are labelled, not erased.
客观措辞是准确事实及注明来源，不是删除错误药量已给入的事实。有依据的临床关注应标明性质，而不是擦掉。

00:21:55.296 --> 00:22:09.888
Complete the separate required safety report and notification. Under current A zero four, PSLS reporting covers clinical deviations, safety events, near misses and errors; it does not replace the PCR.
应另行完成所需安全报告及通知。当前A04要求通过PSLS报告临床偏离、安全事件、险失及错误，但PSLS不能替代PCR。

00:22:09.888 --> 00:22:23.304
Protect privacy through the approved secure channel and actual legal framework. Correct records using the authorized process; do not delete, backdate or rewrite the event to make it appear safer.
应通过批准安全渠道及真实法律框架保护隐私。修正记录须走授权流程，不能删除、倒填时间或改写事件来显得更安全。

00:22:23.304 --> 00:22:35.736
The module names fear of discipline, peer judgment, lack of time and the belief that nothing will change. These are real process barriers, not simply a lack of professional motivation.
模块列出怕处分、怕同伴评价、缺时间，以及觉得不会改变。这些是真实流程障碍，不只是缺职业动力。

00:22:35.736 --> 00:22:47.424
Leaders can make reporting safer by explaining the process, responding fairly and avoiding ridicule. They must not promise immunity that the actual policy cannot guarantee.
负责人可通过说明流程、公正回应及避免嘲讽，使报告更安全，但不能保证真实政策无法保证的免责。

00:22:47.424 --> 00:22:59.520
Make the route clear and accessible, and ensure immediate safety information reaches the right person without waiting for a long form. Complete the required documentation promptly afterward.
应让路径清楚易用，并确保即时安全信息不等长表格就传到正确人员；之后应及时完成所需文书。

00:22:59.520 --> 00:23:10.800
Close the feedback loop with a visible correction and its result. Acknowledging the report without changing a persistent hazard teaches people that reporting has little value.
应以可见修正及结果闭合反馈环。只确认收到，却不处理持续危险，会让人觉得报告无用。

00:23:10.800 --> 00:23:20.592
Build the timeline from actual records and participant accounts. Separate established facts, differing recollections and remaining uncertainty.
应根据真实记录及参与者陈述建立时间线，区分已确认事实、不同回忆及剩余不确定。

00:23:20.592 --> 00:23:27.984
Ask what the provider saw and expected at the time. Avoid assuming that the final outcome was obvious from the beginning.
应问当时看到了什么、预期什么。不能假定最终结局从一开始就显而易见。

00:23:27.984 --> 00:23:39.192
Identify both failed and successful defenses and consider behavior fairly. A near-miss intercept may reveal useful teamwork as well as a system weakness.
应识别失败及成功防御，并公正考虑行为。险失截获既可揭示系统弱点，也可展示有效协作。

00:23:39.192 --> 00:23:50.712
Finish with a practical action, an owner and a way to check change. Offer appropriate support to involved staff without making the debrief a forced personal disclosure exercise.
最后应有实际行动、负责人及检验改变的方法。应支持相关人员，但不能把复盘变成强迫个人情绪披露。

00:23:50.712 --> 00:24:04.488
For the original near miss, propose an approved storage and labelling correction plus a reliable independent check. The correction should address the observed confusion, not merely add a warning to be more careful.
原创险失可提出获批准的存放及标签修正，并配可靠独立核查。修正应针对真实混淆，不只是加一句“更小心”。

00:24:04.488 --> 00:24:16.176
Test it safely with training materials under realistic interruption. Observe whether people identify the right product and detect the mismatch rather than asking whether they like the new system.
应使用训练材料，在真实感的打断条件下安全检验。观察是否选对产品及发现不符，而不只是问是否喜欢新系统。

00:24:16.176 --> 00:24:26.256
Look for unintended consequences such as harder access or a new look-alike arrangement. A locally improved step can still worsen the overall workflow.
应查非预期后果，例如更难取用或形成新的相似排列。局部步骤改善，仍可能让整体工作流变差。

00:24:26.256 --> 00:24:37.152
Record the result and revise the change as needed. Reporting, respectful review and measured correction together create the safer next call described by the module.
应记录结果并按需要修订。报告、尊重审查及有检验的修正结合，才能形成模块所说的下一次更安全出诊。

00:24:37.152 --> 00:24:47.280
Be able to assign roles and update the team when the patient or scene changes. Invite concerns and show that a junior voice can stop an unsafe action.
应能分配角色，并在患者或现场变化时更新团队；邀请关注，并展示新人也能制止不安全行动。

00:24:47.280 --> 00:24:58.944
Demonstrate closed loop, a useful callout, a structured SBAR and appropriate PACE escalation. Do not force a slow sequence when an immediate stop is needed.
应展示闭环、有用紧急通报、结构化SBAR及适当PACE升级。需要立即制止时，不能强迫慢慢走流程。

00:24:58.944 --> 00:25:10.560
Distinguish human error, at-risk behavior and recklessness using evidence and context. Separately identify whether the incident reached the patient and whether harm occurred.
应依据证据及背景区分人为错误、风险行为及鲁莽行为；再另外判断事件是否到达患者，以及是否造成伤害。

00:25:10.560 --> 00:25:23.568
Finally, protect the patient, communicate honestly, complete the correct records and report, then help test a practical improvement. That is the complete safety cycle, not merely a promise to try harder.
最后，应保护患者、诚实沟通、完成正确记录及报告，再协助检验实际改进。这才是完整安全循环，不只是保证以后更努力。
